The plugin holds the page to the schema.org vocabulary, release 30.1, compiled in from
plugins/schema-org/data/vocabulary.json, which is derived from schemaorg-current-https.jsonld
(https://github.com/schemaorg/schemaorg, tag v30.1). The schema.org vocabulary is licensed under
the Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 3.0 Unported licence (CC BY-SA 3.0,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/); see https://schema.org/docs/terms.html. The
derived vocabulary is distributed under the same licence. rBrowser is not affiliated with
schema.org or with Google; the rich-result needs follow Google Search's published documentation.

The plugin's panel (panel/dist/panel.js, panel/dist/panel.css) is built with Vite from web/src
and bundles third-party code unchanged: Vue, Nuxt UI and the packages they use (reka-ui,
TanStack Table, Floating UI, VueUse, tailwind-variants, unhead and others), the compiled styles
of Tailwind CSS, and a selection of Lucide icons (from @iconify-json/lucide). Each is under the
MIT License, Lucide under the ISC License (and the MIT License for the icons derived from
Feather). The name, version and full licence text of every bundled package is in
panel/dist/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, which the build writes beside the panel.
